# CODEOWNERS (#249)
#
# NOTE ON THESE ASSIGNMENTS: every line below points to @bbjiggy. That is a
# placeholder, not a claim that @bbjiggy is the intended long-term owner of
# these paths — actual review ownership is explicitly the maintainers' call,
# not something to decide unilaterally in this change. @bbjiggy is used here
# only because they're the repo's most active contributor/issue author, and
# a CODEOWNERS file with no real entries (or with made-up team names that
# don't exist as GitHub users/teams) wouldn't actually do anything — GitHub
# silently ignores unknown owners. The maintainers should update the owners
# below (ideally to a team, e.g. @ourdao/frontend-maintainers, once one
# exists) to reflect real team structure.
#
# GitHub applies these top-to-bottom with "last match wins", so broad rules
# come first and more specific/sensitive paths are listed after to override
# them.

# Default: anything under src/ not covered by a more specific rule below.
/src/ @bbjiggy

# The only server-side code in this app, and where the Pinata (IPFS) upload
# credential is used — a compromised or careless change here has different
# blast radius than a client component.
/src/app/api/ @bbjiggy

# Freighter integration — the one place the app talks to the wallet
# extension. The app never touches a private key directly (see
# CONTRIBUTING.md), but this file is where that boundary is enforced.
/src/lib/wallet.tsx @bbjiggy

# Contract call signatures and the transaction-signing path. A mismatch here
# vs. the deployed Soroban contract fails at signature time for a real
# member, not in CI.
/src/lib/dao-client.ts @bbjiggy

# Security headers (CSP, HSTS, frame-ancestors, etc.) for the whole app.
/next.config.ts @bbjiggy
